    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Analyzing the reviews per month and review scores to gauge interaction patterns among hosts. Hosts with higher reviews per month could be considered as more connected or influential, as their interactions with guests are more frequent."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IShPYfBytboi"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# 1. Analyze the Relationship Between Reviews and Host Listings\n",
        "# We’ll first identify which hosts have the most active reviews, and then link it to the number of listings they manage to see if more listings correlate with higher guest engagement.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Group by host listings count to see if there's a correlation with reviews per month\n",
        "host_reviews = df[['id', 'calculated_host_listings_count', 'reviews_per_month']].dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate average reviews per host\n",
        "host_reviews_avg = host_reviews.groupby('calculated_host_listings_count').agg(\n",
        "    avg_reviews_per_month=('reviews_per_month', 'mean')\n",
        ").reset_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot the relationship between the number of listings and reviews per month\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "plt.scatter(host_reviews_avg['calculated_host_listings_count'], host_reviews_avg['avg_reviews_per_month'])\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Number of Listings')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Average Reviews per Month')\n",
        "plt.title('Reviews per Month vs Number of Listings per Host')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
