    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. clustering to find groups of hosts who have similar features, such as the number of listings they manage, price ranges, and review scores. These clusters may represent different \"communities\" of hosts that interact with guests in similar ways (e.g., luxury vs budget listings, superhosts vs regular hosts)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3bXo6ugAt06n"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "# Select relevant columns for clustering (price, reviews per month, host listings count)\n",
        "cluster_data = df[['price', 'reviews_per_month', 'calculated_host_listings_count']].dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Normalize the data\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "scaled_data = scaler.fit_transform(cluster_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply KMeans clustering\n",
        "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=5, random_state=42)  # 5 clusters as an example\n",
        "cluster_data['cluster'] = kmeans.fit_predict(scaled_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualize the clusters\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "plt.scatter(cluster_data['price'], cluster_data['reviews_per_month'], c=cluster_data['cluster'], cmap='viridis')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Price')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Reviews per Month')\n",
        "plt.title('Clustering Hosts by Price and Reviews per Month')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
